  83: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  84:     """
  85:     Swap a connector segment with repeated marker sprites by connecting the marker anchors and stamping the sprite at the segment endpoints.
  86: 
  87:     Input structure
  88:     The grid has one background color and exactly two foreground colors. One foreground color forms a single straight 8-connected segment. The other foreground color forms two or more identical centered sprites.
  89: 
  90:     Rule
  91:     Build a background canvas of the same size. Draw straight connector-color segments between every pair of original sprite anchors. Then stamp the marker sprite, using its centered anchor, onto the two endpoints of the original connector segment.
  92: 
  93:     Key insight
  94:     The original segment endpoints are the destinations for the repeated sprite, while the original sprite centers become the vertices of the new connector-color complete graph.
  95:     """
  96:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  97:     bg = get_bg(g)
  98:     colors = colors_present(g, exclude={bg})
  99:     assert len(colors) == 2
 100: 
